#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ccfleet -- run headless Claude Code sessions across a fleet of repos, each
one billed to its own repo, started only while the machine has headroom.

Why it exists: per-repo cost tools (`ccrepo`) label usage by the session's
working-directory basename. A subagent started with the Agent tool runs in its
parent's directory, so work done "for" another repo by an Agent subagent bills
the orchestrator's repo, not the repo it was for. The fix is structural: each
repo's work runs as its own `claude -p` session started INSIDE a worktree of
that repo whose basename is the repo name. Doing that by hand for a dozen repos,
without crashing the machine, is what this instrument does.

THE LESSONS IT CARRIES (each one paid for in a real run):
  * `claude -p` is always started with stdin from /dev/null. Without it a
    "no stdin" warning lands in the JSON log and the result cannot be parsed.
  * Every launch names its model (`--model`). A launch without one silently
    inherits the default tier; tools/modelguard.py blocks such launches.
  * The worktree's basename is the repo name, under a per-job parent directory
    (`<worktrees_root>/<label>-<HHMM>/<repo>`). That basename is the billing key.
  * Never repo work as an Agent subagent of the orchestrator (see above).
  * A public repo's prompt never names a private repo. Rendering refuses to
    launch a prompt for a public (or unknown-visibility) repo that contains any
    configured private name. The guard is a literal match, so it catches the
    names you list and nothing you forgot to list.
  * This is Python, not zsh, on purpose: zsh reads a script as it runs, so
    editing a driver script mid-run broke every running job's tail. Python
    compiles the whole file at start, so a running driver is immune; a job
    started after an edit runs the edited copy.
  * Start one job at a time, staggered, and only while load, free memory and
    free disk all have headroom: parallel test runs inside headless sessions
    have taken a 16 GB laptop past load 100. Workers run their own tests
    niced and single-process; say so in the prompt.
  * A run past a usage limit ends with no RESULT line (read as UNKNOWN). The
    drain stops after three unclean ends in a row, which is how a spent budget
    shows up from outside.
  * A `touch <kit_dir>/stop` ends launching cleanly; running jobs finish.

Usage:
  ccfleet check                       validate the config and print what it resolves to
  ccfleet gate                        print the headroom reading; exit 0 if a start may go now
  ccfleet run REPO --prompt FILE [--label L] [--model M] [--set K=V ...] [--keep] [--in WT] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet drive JOBS [--max N] [--serial-per-repo] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet drain [--max N] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet pass REPO ITEM BRIEF [--dry-run]      one drain pass (drain starts these)
  ccfleet resume REPO WORKTREE SESSION --prompt FILE [--item ITEM] [--set K=V ...]
  common: --config PATH (else $CCFLEET_CONFIG)  --by ID (else $CCFLEET_BY): the
  orchestrating session's id, filled into prompts as {BY}.

JOBS is a TSV file, one job per line: repo, label, prompt template, then any
number of KEY=VALUE fields that fill {KEY} in that template (MODEL=<id> sets the
model; a value written @file:PATH takes that file's text, for a multi-line task). '#' lines and blank lines are skipped. A job whose result file for today
already exists is skipped, so re-running a drive resumes it.

CONFIG is JSON (see instruments/ccfleet.example.json, every value fictional):
  kit_dir         logs/, results/<date>/, scratch/<repo>/, the stop file   (required)
  repos_root      primary checkouts live at <repos_root>/<repo>          (required)
  worktrees_root  job worktrees go under here                            (required)
  default_model   the model a job runs on when neither job nor repo names one (required)
  claude_bin      default "claude";   claude_args  extra args, e.g. a permission mode
  nice            default 5;  max_concurrent  default 4;  stagger_seconds  default 90;  poll_seconds 30
  gate            {max_load (default 2 x cores), min_mem_pct 25, min_disk_gb 20}
  reset_utc       "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM": no new start at or after it (a budget reset)
  private_names   names a public repo's prompt must never contain
  vars            template variables for every job (the principal's words, paths)
  repos           {name: {model, notes, visibility, github}}  per-repo facts
  queue           drain only: {next, take, release} argv lists (see below)
  pass_prompt     drain only: the per-pass orchestrator prompt template
  pass_model      drain only: the orchestrator's model (the reviewer's tier is the prompt's business)

THE QUEUE INTERFACE (drain). The review queue itself is the adopter's own tool;
ccfleet only calls it. Each entry is an argv list; {REPO} {ITEM} {BRIEF} {BY}
{WT} {LOG} are filled in before the call.
  next     prints "REPO ITEM BRIEF_RELPATH" for the next pass to run, or nothing
           when the queue is empty. It is called with the launched list's path
           in {LAUNCHED} (one "REPO ITEM BRIEF" per line) so it can skip them.
  take     claims the pass; a nonzero exit means someone else holds it (skip).
  release  frees the claim after a pass ends DONE or SKIPPED.

Template variables always filled: {REPO} {GH} {BR} {VIS} {PIN} {WT} {PRIMARY}
{LANDING} {NOTES} {SCRATCH} {BY} {DATE}, plus config `vars`, plus the job's own.
A {UPPER_CASE} placeholder left unfilled is a refusal, not a silent gap.

Exit codes: 0 ran (the session's own verdict is in its END line and result
file) · 1 setup failed · 2 claim refused · 3 reset reached · 4 queue empty ·
5 refused by the private-name guard or an unfilled placeholder · 64 usage.
Runtime: Python 3.8 or later, standard library only; git on PATH; gh optional
(visibility lookup when a repo's config does not state it).
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

EXIT_SETUP, EXIT_CLAIM, EXIT_RESET, EXIT_EMPTY, EXIT_GUARD, EXIT_USAGE = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 64
PLACEHOLDER = re.compile(r"\{([A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*)\}")
RESULT_RX = re.compile(r"RESULT:\s*\**\s*([A-Z]+(?: [A-Z]+)?)")


class Refusal(Exception):
    def __init__(self, code, msg):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.code = code


def now_utc():
    return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)


def expand(p):
    return os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(p)) if p else p


# ---------- config ----------

def load_config(path):
    path = path or os.environ.get("CCFLEET_CONFIG")
    if not path:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "no config: pass --config PATH or set CCFLEET_CONFIG")
    with open(expand(path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        cfg = json.load(f)
    missing = [k for k in ("kit_dir", "repos_root", "worktrees_root", "default_model") if not cfg.get(k)]
    if missing:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"config {path}: missing {', '.join(missing)}")
    for k in ("kit_dir", "repos_root", "worktrees_root"):
        cfg[k] = expand(cfg[k])
    cfg.setdefault("claude_bin", "claude")
    cfg.setdefault("claude_args", [])
    cfg.setdefault("nice", 5)
    cfg.setdefault("max_concurrent", 4)
    cfg.setdefault("stagger_seconds", 90)
    cfg.setdefault("poll_seconds", 30)
    gate = cfg.setdefault("gate", {})
    gate.setdefault("max_load", 2 * (os.cpu_count() or 4))
    gate.setdefault("min_mem_pct", 25)
    gate.setdefault("min_disk_gb", 20)
    cfg.setdefault("private_names", [])
    cfg.setdefault("vars", {})
    cfg.setdefault("repos", {})
    return cfg


def reset_reached(cfg, at=None):
    r = cfg.get("reset_utc")
    if not r:
        return False
    when = dt.datetime.strptime(r, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M").replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc)
    return (at or now_utc()) >= when


# ---------- headroom gate ----------

def read_mem_pct():
    """Free memory as a percentage, or None when it cannot be read."""
    if sys.platform == "darwin":
        try:
            out = subprocess.run(["memory_pressure", "-Q"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout
            m = re.search(r"free percentage:\s*(\d+)", out)
            return int(m.group(1)) if m else None
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return None
    try:
        info = {}
        with open("/proc/meminfo") as f:
            for line in f:
                k, v = line.split(":", 1)
                info[k] = int(v.split()[0])
        return int(100 * info["MemAvailable"] / info["MemTotal"])
    except (OSError, KeyError, ValueError):
        return None


def read_headroom(cfg):
    l1, l5, l15 = os.getloadavg()
    probe = cfg["worktrees_root"]
    while not os.path.exists(probe):
        probe = os.path.dirname(probe)
    disk_gb = shutil.disk_usage(probe).free // 2**30
    return {"load": (l1, l5, l15), "mem_pct": read_mem_pct(), "disk_gb": disk_gb}


def gate_ok(gate, reading):
    """A start may go only when every reading has headroom. An unreadable
    memory figure holds (fail closed) unless min_mem_pct is 0."""
    l1, l5, _ = reading["load"]
    if l1 >= gate["max_load"] or l5 >= gate["max_load"]:
        return False
    if gate["min_mem_pct"] > 0 and (reading["mem_pct"] is None or reading["mem_pct"] < gate["min_mem_pct"]):
        return False
    return reading["disk_gb"] >= gate["min_disk_gb"]


def describe(reading):
    l = reading["load"]
    mem = "?" if reading["mem_pct"] is None else reading["mem_pct"]
    return f"load {l[0]:.1f}/{l[1]:.1f}/{l[2]:.1f} mem {mem}% disk {reading['disk_gb']}G"


# ---------- git facts ----------

def git(*args, cwd=None, check=True):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", *args], cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"git {' '.join(args)}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return r.stdout.strip()


def repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=True):
    primary = os.path.join(cfg["repos_root"], repo)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(primary, ".git")) and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(primary, ".git")):
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"not a git checkout: {primary}")
    rc = cfg["repos"].get(repo, {})
    remote = git("remote", "get-url", "origin", cwd=primary, check=False)
    facts = {"primary": primary, "remote": bool(remote)}
    if remote:
        if fetch:
            git("fetch", "-q", "origin", cwd=primary)
        # Not every repo's mainline is main.
        ref = git("symbolic-ref", "--short", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD", cwd=primary, check=False)
        facts["defref"] = ref or "origin/main"
        facts["branch"] = facts["defref"].split("/", 1)[1]
        m = re.search(r"github\.com[:/](.+?)(?:\.git)?$", remote)
        facts["gh"] = rc.get("github") or (m.group(1) if m else remote)
    else:
        facts["defref"] = facts["branch"] = rc.get("branch", "main")
        facts["gh"] = rc.get("github", "(no remote)")
    vis = rc.get("visibility")
    if not vis and remote and shutil.which("gh") and fetch:
        r = subprocess.run(["gh", "repo", "view", facts["gh"], "--json", "visibility", "-q", ".visibility"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        vis = r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else None
    facts["visibility"] = (vis or "UNKNOWN").upper()
    return facts


def landing_text(facts, wt, branch_name=None):
    if facts["remote"]:
        b = facts["branch"]
        return (f"Land each commit with `git -C '{wt}' pull --rebase origin {b}` then "
                f"`git -C '{wt}' push origin HEAD:{b}` (unless this repo's CLAUDE.md requires "
                f"a PR; then open one and say so).")
    return (f"This repo has NO remote; local {facts['branch']} is the mainline and your worktree is on "
            f"branch {branch_name}. Instead of pull/push: `git -C '{wt}' rebase {facts['branch']}`, then land "
            f"with `git -C '{facts['primary']}' merge --ff-only {branch_name}` against the primary checkout "
            f"(only while it is on {facts['branch']}; if the merge refuses over uncommitted changes there, "
            f"wait and retry, never stash or absorb them). Never `git push`.")


# ---------- prompt rendering ----------

def render(template, values):
    out = PLACEHOLDER.sub(lambda m: str(values[m.group(1)]) if m.group(1) in values else m.group(0), template)
    left = sorted(set(PLACEHOLDER.findall(out)))
    return out, left


def private_hits(cfg, text, visibility):
    """Private names in a prompt bound for a public or unknown-visibility repo."""
    if visibility == "PRIVATE":
        return []
    names = set(cfg["private_names"])
    names |= {r for r, rc in cfg["repos"].items() if str(rc.get("visibility", "")).upper() == "PRIVATE"}
    return sorted(n for n in names if re.search(r"(?<![\w-])" + re.escape(n) + r"(?![\w-])", text, re.I))


def build_prompt(cfg, template_path, values):
    with open(expand(template_path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        text, left = render(f.read(), values)
    if left:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_GUARD, f"unfilled placeholder(s) in {template_path}: {', '.join('{'+k+'}' for k in left)}")
    hits = private_hits(cfg, text, values.get("VIS", "UNKNOWN"))
    if hits:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_GUARD, f"refused: the prompt for {values.get('REPO')} ({values.get('VIS')}) names "
                                  f"private name(s) {', '.join(hits)}")
    return text


# ---------- one session ----------

def harvest(log_path):
    """(result text, session id, RESULT word) from a `claude -p --output-format json` log."""
    try:
        with open(log_path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            s = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return "", "", "UNKNOWN"
    try:
        j = json.loads(s[s.index("{"):])
        text, sid = j.get("result", "") or "", j.get("session_id", "") or ""
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        text, sid = s[-4000:], ""
    found = RESULT_RX.findall(text)
    return text, sid, (found[-1] if found else "UNKNOWN")


def stamp_dir(root, label):
    stamp = now_utc().strftime("%H%M")
    parent = os.path.join(root, f"{label}-{stamp}")
    if os.path.exists(parent):
        parent += now_utc().strftime("%S")
    return parent


def session_argv(cfg, model, prompt, resume=None):
    argv = []
    if cfg["nice"]:
        argv += ["nice", "-n", str(cfg["nice"])]
    argv += [cfg["claude_bin"], "-p"]
    if resume:
        argv += ["--resume", resume]
    argv += ["--model", model, *cfg["claude_args"], "--output-format", "json", prompt]
    return argv


def launch(cfg, argv, cwd, log):
    # stdin from /dev/null, always: see the module docstring.
    with open(log, "w") as out, open(log + ".err", "w") as err:
        return subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=out, stderr=err).returncode


def read_at_file(v):
    """A variable written `@file:PATH` takes the file's text (a multi-line task)."""
    if isinstance(v, str) and v.startswith("@file:"):
        with open(expand(v[6:]), encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return f.read().rstrip("\n")
    return v


def safe(s):
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]+", "-", s).strip("-")


def run_one(cfg, repo, template, label=None, model=None, extra=None, by="unknown",
            dry=False, keep=False, pre=None, post=None, check_file=None, existing=None):
    """Make the worktree, render, launch, harvest, clean up. Returns (exit, RESULT word)."""
    if reset_reached(cfg):
        print(f"RESET reached; not starting {label or repo}")
        return EXIT_RESET, "RESET"
    extra = {k: read_at_file(v) for k, v in (extra or {}).items()}
    model = model or extra.pop("MODEL", None) or cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("model") or cfg["default_model"]
    label = safe(label or repo)
    facts = repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=not dry)
    day = now_utc().strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    wt = expand(existing) if existing else os.path.join(stamp_dir(cfg["worktrees_root"], label), repo)
    if existing and (os.path.basename(wt) != repo or not os.path.isdir(wt)):
        # The basename is the billing key: a session in a differently named
        # directory would bill some other label.
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"--in must be an existing worktree whose basename is {repo}: {wt}")
    keep = keep or bool(existing)  # an adopted worktree is the caller's to remove
    kit = cfg["kit_dir"]
    logs, results, scratch = (os.path.join(kit, "logs"), os.path.join(kit, "results", day),
                              os.path.join(kit, "scratch", safe(repo)))
    log = os.path.join(logs, os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(wt))
                       + (f"-in-{now_utc():%H%M%S}" if existing else "") + ".json")
    branch_name = None if (facts["remote"] or existing) else f"fleet/{label}-{now_utc().strftime('%H%M%S')}"
    values = {**{k: str(v) for k, v in cfg["vars"].items()}, **{k: str(v) for k, v in extra.items()},
              "REPO": repo, "GH": facts["gh"], "BR": facts["branch"], "VIS": facts["visibility"],
              "WT": wt, "PRIMARY": facts["primary"], "LANDING": landing_text(facts, wt, branch_name),
              "NOTES": cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("notes", "none"), "SCRATCH": scratch + "/",
              "BY": by, "DATE": day}
    values.setdefault("PIN", "")
    prompt = build_prompt(cfg, template, values)
    argv = session_argv(cfg, model, prompt)
    if dry:
        print(f"DRY {repo} model={model} vis={facts['visibility']} wt={wt}")
        print(f"DRY worktree add from {facts['defref']}; log={log}")
        print("DRY argv: " + " ".join(argv[:-1]) + f" <prompt {len(prompt)} chars> < /dev/null")
        return 0, "DRY"
    for d in (logs, results, scratch, os.path.dirname(wt)):
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    if existing:
        pass
    elif facts["remote"]:
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", "--detach", wt, facts["defref"], cwd=facts["primary"])
    else:
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", "-b", branch_name, wt, facts["branch"], cwd=facts["primary"])

    def cleanup():
        git("worktree", "remove", "--force", wt, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)
        try:
            os.rmdir(os.path.dirname(wt))
        except OSError:
            pass
        if branch_name:
            git("branch", "-d", branch_name, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)

    if check_file and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(wt, check_file)):
        print(f"not on {facts['defref']}: {check_file}")
        cleanup()
        return EXIT_SETUP, "UNKNOWN"
    if pre:
        code = pre(values, log)
        if code:
            cleanup()
            return code, "UNKNOWN"
    print(f"START {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} {label} model={model} wt={wt} log={log}", flush=True)
    rc = launch(cfg, argv, wt, log)
    text, sid, result = harvest(log)
    out = os.path.join(results, f"{label}.md")
    with open(out, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(f"<!-- session {sid} -->\n{text}\n")
    print(f"END {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} rc={rc} result={result} session={sid} out={out}", flush=True)
    finished = result in ("DONE", "SKIPPED")
    if post:
        post(values, finished, sid)
    if not keep and (finished or not post):
        cleanup()
    return 0, result


# ---------- drivers ----------

class DriverLock:
    """One driver per kit_dir: two drivers would each think they own the slots."""

    def __init__(self, kit):
        self.path = os.path.join(kit, "driver.pid")

    def __enter__(self):
        if os.path.exists(self.path):
            try:
                with open(self.path) as f:
                    pid = int(f.read().strip())
                os.kill(pid, 0)
                raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"another driver (pid {pid}) is running on this kit_dir")
            except (ValueError, ProcessLookupError):
                pass
        with open(self.path, "w") as f:
            f.write(str(os.getpid()))
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        try:
            os.remove(self.path)
        except OSError:
            pass


def say(cfg, msg):
    with open(os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "driver.log"), "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{now_utc():%H:%MZ} {msg}\n")


def read_jobs(path):
    jobs = []
    with open(expand(path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        lines = f.read().splitlines()
    for n, line in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not line.strip() or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        f = line.split("\t")
        if len(f) < 3:
            raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"{path}:{n}: need repo, label, prompt")
        extra = dict(x.split("=", 1) for x in f[3:] if "=" in x)
        jobs.append({"repo": f[0], "label": safe(f[1] or f[0]), "prompt": f[2], "vars": extra})
    return jobs


def self_argv(args_common, *rest):
    return [sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), *args_common, *rest]


def drive(cfg, jobs, common, max_n, serial_per_repo, dry):
    """Start jobs in order, up to max_n at once, one per stagger, only with headroom.
    serial_per_repo: never two jobs of one repo at once (one writer per repo)."""
    kit, day = cfg["kit_dir"], now_utc().strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(kit, "logs"), exist_ok=True)
    queue, running, last_hold = list(jobs), {}, 0
    say(cfg, f"drive up: {len(queue)} jobs, max {max_n}{', serial per repo' if serial_per_repo else ''}")
    while queue or running:
        for p in [p for p in running if p.poll() is not None]:
            say(cfg, f"done {running.pop(p)['label']} rc={p.returncode}")
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(kit, "stop")) and queue:
            say(cfg, f"stop file: {len(queue)} jobs not started")
            queue = []
        busy = {j["repo"] for j in running.values()}
        nxt = next((j for j in queue if not (serial_per_repo and j["repo"] in busy)), None)
        if nxt and os.path.exists(os.path.join(kit, "results", day, nxt["label"] + ".md")):
            queue.remove(nxt)
            say(cfg, f"skip {nxt['label']} (result exists for {day})")
            continue
        if nxt and len(running) < max_n:
            reading = read_headroom(cfg)
            if gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading) or dry:
                queue.remove(nxt)
                rest = ["run", nxt["repo"], "--prompt", nxt["prompt"], "--label", nxt["label"]]
                for k, v in nxt["vars"].items():
                    rest += ["--set", f"{k}={v}"]
                if dry:
                    rest.append("--dry-run")
                with open(os.path.join(kit, "logs", f"run-{nxt['label']}.out"), "w") as out:
                    p = subprocess.Popen(self_argv(common, *rest), stdout=out, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
                running[p] = nxt
                say(cfg, f"start {nxt['label']} ({len(running)}/{max_n}, {describe(reading)})")
                if not dry:
                    time.sleep(cfg["stagger_seconds"])
                continue
            if time.time() - last_hold > 600:
                say(cfg, f"holding: {describe(reading)}")
                last_hold = time.time()
        time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
    say(cfg, "drive down")


def queue_call(cfg, name, values):
    argv = [os.path.expanduser(PLACEHOLDER.sub(lambda m: str(values.get(m.group(1), m.group(0))), a))
            for a in cfg["queue"][name]]
    return subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True)


def drain(cfg, common, max_n, dry):
    """Keep up to max_n review passes running from the adopter's queue until it is
    empty, the reset arrives, the stop file appears, or the budget runs out."""
    if not cfg.get("queue") or not all(k in cfg["queue"] for k in ("next", "take", "release")):
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "drain needs queue.next, queue.take and queue.release in the config")
    kit = cfg["kit_dir"]
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(kit, "logs"), exist_ok=True)
    launched = os.path.join(kit, f"launched-{now_utc():%Y-%m-%d}.txt")
    open(launched, "a").close()
    running, bad, stop, empty, last_hold = {}, 0, None, False, 0
    say(cfg, f"drain up: max {max_n}, gate {cfg['gate']}")
    while True:
        for p in [p for p in running if p.poll() is not None]:
            pick, out = running.pop(p)
            empty = False  # a slot freed: the queue may have something again
            with open(out, errors="replace") as f:
                end = [l for l in f if l.startswith("END ")]
            if p.returncode == EXIT_RESET:
                stop = stop or "reset"
            elif not end:
                say(cfg, f"{pick} ended early rc={p.returncode}")
            else:
                say(cfg, f"{pick} {end[-1].strip()}")
                if "result=DONE" in end[-1] or "result=SKIPPED" in end[-1]:
                    bad = 0
                elif "result=BUDGET EXHAUSTED" in end[-1]:
                    stop = "budget"
                else:
                    bad += 1
                    stop = stop or ("failures" if bad >= 3 else None)
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(kit, "stop")):
            stop = stop or "stopfile"
        if reset_reached(cfg):
            stop = stop or "reset"
        if stop or empty:
            if not running:
                break
            time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
            continue
        if len(running) < max_n:
            reading = read_headroom(cfg)
            if gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading) or dry:
                r = queue_call(cfg, "next", {"LAUNCHED": launched, "BY": common_by(common)})
                pick = r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1].split() if r.stdout.strip() else []
                if len(pick) < 3:
                    empty = True
                    say(cfg, "queue: nothing launchable now")
                    continue
                with open(launched, "a") as f:
                    f.write(" ".join(pick[:3]) + "\n")
                out = os.path.join(kit, "logs", f"pass-{safe(pick[0] + '-' + pick[1])}-{now_utc():%H%M%S}.out")
                rest = ["pass", *pick[:3]] + (["--dry-run"] if dry else [])
                with open(out, "w") as fh:
                    p = subprocess.Popen(self_argv(common, *rest), stdout=fh, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
                running[p] = (" ".join(pick[:2]), out)
                say(cfg, f"started {pick[0]} {pick[1]} ({len(running)}/{max_n}, {describe(reading)})")
                if not dry:
                    time.sleep(cfg["stagger_seconds"])
                continue
            if time.time() - last_hold > 600:
                say(cfg, f"holding starts: {describe(reading)}")
                last_hold = time.time()
        time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
    say(cfg, f"drain down: {stop or 'queue empty'}")
    print(f"DRAIN EXIT: {stop or 'queue empty'}")


def common_by(common):
    return common[common.index("--by") + 1] if "--by" in common else "unknown"


def one_pass(cfg, repo, item, brief, by, dry):
    """One review pass: worktree, claim, the orchestrator session, release on a clean end."""
    template = cfg.get("pass_prompt")
    if not template:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "pass needs pass_prompt (the orchestrator prompt template) in the config")
    label = safe(f"{repo}-{item}")

    def pre(values, log):
        r = queue_call(cfg, "take", {**values, "ITEM": item, "BRIEF": brief, "LOG": log})
        if r.returncode:
            print(f"claim refused: {r.stdout.strip()} {r.stderr.strip()}")
            return EXIT_CLAIM
        return 0

    def post(values, finished, sid):
        if finished:
            queue_call(cfg, "release", {**values, "ITEM": item, "BRIEF": brief, "SESSION": sid})

    return run_one(cfg, repo, expand(template), label=label, model=cfg.get("pass_model"),
                   extra={"ITEM": item, "BRIEF": brief}, by=by, dry=dry,
                   pre=None if dry else pre, post=None if dry else post, check_file=brief)[0]


def resume(cfg, repo, wt, sid, template, item, extra, by):
    """Finish one pass a usage limit cut off: resume its own session, start nothing new."""
    model = cfg.get("pass_model") or cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("model") or cfg["default_model"]
    facts = repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=False)
    values = {**{k: str(v) for k, v in cfg["vars"].items()}, **extra, "REPO": repo, "WT": wt, "SESSION": sid,
              "ITEM": item or "", "BY": by, "VIS": facts["visibility"], "GH": facts["gh"],
              "BR": facts["branch"], "LANDING": landing_text(facts, wt, None), "DATE": f"{now_utc():%Y-%m-%d}"}
    prompt = build_prompt(cfg, template, values)
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "logs"), exist_ok=True)
    log = os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "logs", f"resume-{safe(repo + '-' + (item or sid))}-{now_utc():%H%M}.json")
    print(f"START {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} resume {repo} {item or ''} of {sid}", flush=True)
    rc = launch(cfg, session_argv(cfg, model, prompt, resume=sid), wt, log)
    _, _, result = harvest(log)
    print(f"END {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} rc={rc} result={result}", flush=True)
    if result == "DONE" and item and cfg.get("queue", {}).get("release"):
        queue_call(cfg, "release", {**values, "BRIEF": ""})
        git("worktree", "remove", "--force", wt, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)
    return 0


# ---------- CLI ----------

def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="ccfleet", description="Per-repo billed headless sessions across a fleet, "
                                 "load-gated. Full reference: the module docstring (ccfleet --doc).")
    ap.add_argument("--config")
    ap.add_argument("--by", default=os.environ.get("CCFLEET_BY", "unknown"))
    ap.add_argument("--doc", action="store_true", help="print the full reference and exit")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    sub.add_parser("check")
    sub.add_parser("gate")
    p = sub.add_parser("run")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("--prompt", required=True); p.add_argument("--label")
    p.add_argument("--model"); p.add_argument("--set", action="append", default=[]); p.add_argument("--keep", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--in", dest="existing", metavar="WT")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("drive")
    p.add_argument("jobs"); p.add_argument("--max", type=int); p.add_argument("--serial-per-repo", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("drain")
    p.add_argument("--max", type=int); p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("pass")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("item"); p.add_argument("brief"); p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("resume")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("worktree"); p.add_argument("session"); p.add_argument("--prompt", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--item"); p.add_argument("--set", action="append", default=[])
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if a.doc:
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    if not a.cmd:
        ap.print_help()
        return EXIT_USAGE
    try:
        cfg = load_config(a.config)
        common = (["--config", a.config] if a.config else []) + ["--by", a.by]
        if a.cmd == "check":
            print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in cfg.items() if k != "vars"}, indent=1))
            print(f"vars: {', '.join(sorted(cfg['vars'])) or 'none'}; reset reached: {reset_reached(cfg)}")
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "gate":
            reading = read_headroom(cfg)
            ok = gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading)
            print(f"{'go' if ok else 'hold'}: {describe(reading)} (gate {cfg['gate']})")
            return 0 if ok else 1
        if a.cmd == "run":
            extra = dict(s.split("=", 1) for s in a.set)
            return run_one(cfg, a.repo, a.prompt, label=a.label, model=a.model, extra=extra, by=a.by,
                           dry=a.dry_run, keep=a.keep, existing=a.existing)[0]
        if a.cmd == "drive":
            with DriverLock(cfg["kit_dir"]):
                drive(cfg, read_jobs(a.jobs), common, a.max or cfg["max_concurrent"], a.serial_per_repo, a.dry_run)
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "drain":
            with DriverLock(cfg["kit_dir"]):
                drain(cfg, common, a.max or cfg["max_concurrent"], a.dry_run)
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "pass":
            return one_pass(cfg, a.repo, a.item, a.brief, a.by, a.dry_run)
        if a.cmd == "resume":
            return resume(cfg, a.repo, expand(a.worktree), a.session, a.prompt, a.item,
                          dict(s.split("=", 1) for s in a.set), a.by)
    except Refusal as e:
        print(f"ccfleet: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code
    return EXIT_USAGE


if __name__ == "__main__":
    signal.signal(signal.SIGPIPE, signal.SIG_DFL)
    sys.exit(main())
